["How much does a home battery cost in Pennsylvania?", "EnergySage reports an average of $17,550 for a 13 kWh battery installed in Pennsylvania before incentives, or about $1,350 per kWh, with a typical range of $14,918 to $20,182 (page updated November 15, 2026)."],
["Are there battery rebates in Pennsylvania?", "We haven't found one as of November 23, 2026. Pennsylvania's federally funded Penn Energy Savers rebates (HOMES and HEEHR, formerly HEAR) have not launched; the program site lists them as coming soon in spring 2027, and they are for efficient electric appliances and efficiency upgrades, not batteries. The federal 25D battery tax credit ended for installs completed after 12/31/2025."],
["How often does the power go out in Pennsylvania?", "EIA reports the average Pennsylvania customer was without power for 458.1 minutes (about 7.6 hours) in 2025 including major events, versus 262.6 minutes for the U.S. as a whole. Without major events it was 132.8 minutes. Customers averaged about 1.4 interruptions."],
